IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`

-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (United Kingdom), 1992 c. 4.
-- SCHEDULE 9 (exclusions from entitlement to child benefit) and SCHEDULE 10 (priority between persons entitled to child benefit).
-- The converter dropped the paragraph numbers. Schedule 9 has five headings: 1 Children and qualifying young persons in detention, care, etc.;
-- 2 a heading shown as "..." with a row of dots (repealed or blank); 3 Married children and qualifying young persons; 4 Persons exempt from tax
-- and 5 Children entitled to severe disablement allowance (both dots only). Schedule 10 has six: 1 Person with prior award, 2 Person having child
-- or qualifying young person living with him, 3 Opposite-sex spouses or civil partners, 4 Parents, 5 Other cases, 6 Supplementary. The text's own citations
-- confirm 1 to 6 ("paragraph 1 above" in 2; "paragraphs 1 and 2 above" in 3; "paragraphs 1 to 3 above" in 4; "paragraphs 1 to 4 above" in 5; "paragraphs 1 to 5 above" in 6).
-- Schedule 10 is asked about two people: the person asking and the other. Each priority rule answers for the person asking: JUST TRUE when it makes them the
-- one entitled, JUST FALSE when it makes the other the one entitled, NOTHING when the paragraph does not decide (it does not apply, or an earlier paragraph decides).

§ `Schedule 9 -- exclusions from entitlement to child benefit`

§§ `Paragraph 1 -- children and qualifying young persons in detention, care, etc.`

-- 1: "Except where regulations otherwise provide, no person shall be entitled to child benefit in respect of a child or qualifying young person for any week
-- if in that week the child or qualifying young person" (a) is undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody, (b) is subject to a compulsory supervision
-- order (within section 83 of the Children's Hearings (Scotland) Act 2011) and is residing in a residential establishment (within section 202(1) of that Act),
-- or (c) is in the care of a local authority in such circumstances as may be prescribed. The two Scottish terms are borrowed, so each answer is an input.
-- src:5643 | Except where regulations otherwise provide, no person shall be entitled to child benefit in respect of a child or qualifying young person for any week if in that week the child or qualifying young person—
-- src:5644 | (a) is undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody;
-- src:5645 | (b) is subject to a compulsory supervision order (within the meaning of section 83 of the Children’s Hearings (Scotland) Act 2011) and is residing in a residential establishment (within the meaning of section 202(1) of that Act); or
-- src:5646 | (c) is in the care of a local authority in such circumstances as may be prescribed.
@ref sch 9 para 1 (src:5643-5646)
GIVEN `the child or qualifying young person is undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody in the week` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the child or qualifying young person is subject to a compulsory supervision order (within the meaning of section 83 of the Children’s Hearings (Scotland) Act 2011) and is residing in a residential establishment (within the meaning of section 202(1) of that Act) in the week` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the child or qualifying young person is in the care of a local authority in the week in circumstances which are prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulations otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 1 the person may be entitled to child benefit for the week` MEANS
    IF (`the child or qualifying young person is undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody in the week` OR `the child or qualifying young person is subject to a compulsory supervision order (within the meaning of section 83 of the Children’s Hearings (Scotland) Act 2011) and is residing in a residential establishment (within the meaning of section 202(1) of that Act) in the week` OR `the child or qualifying young person is in the care of a local authority in the week in circumstances which are prescribed`) AND NOT `regulations otherwise provide`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no person shall be entitled to child benefit in respect of a child or qualifying young person for any week if in that week ..."
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "no person shall be entitled ... if" is a bar and no grant; section 142 and the rest of Part IX decide

§§ `Paragraph 3 -- married children and qualifying young persons`

-- 3: "Except where regulations otherwise provide, no person shall be entitled to child benefit in respect of a child or qualifying young person who is married or is a civil partner."
-- src:5650 | Except where regulations otherwise provide, no person shall be entitled to child benefit in respect of a child or qualifying young person who is married or is a civil partner.
@ref sch 9 para 3 (src:5650)
GIVEN `the child or qualifying young person is married or is a civil partner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulations otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 9 para 3 the person may be entitled to child benefit for the child or qualifying young person` MEANS
    IF `the child or qualifying young person is married or is a civil partner` AND NOT `regulations otherwise provide`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no person shall be entitled to child benefit in respect of a child or qualifying young person who is married or is a civil partner"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a bar and no grant

§ `Schedule 10 -- priority between persons entitled to child benefit`

§§ `Paragraph 1 -- person with prior award`

DECLARE `sch 10 para 1 Place` IS ONE OF
    `sch 10 para 1 the person has already been awarded child benefit when the other claims`
    `sch 10 para 1 the person is the one claiming`

-- 1(1) and (2): as between a person claiming child benefit for a child or qualifying young person for a week and a person to whom it has already been awarded for that
-- week when the claim is made, "the latter shall be entitled", subject to (2): no priority where the week to which the claim relates is later than the third week
-- following that in which the claim is made.
-- src:5657 | (1) Subject to sub-paragraph (2) below, as between a person claiming child benefit in respect of a child or qualifying young person for any week and a person to whom child benefit in respect of that child or qualifying young person for that week has already been awarded when the claim is made, the latter shall be entitled.
-- src:5658 | (2) Sub-paragraph (1) above shall not confer any priority where the week to which the claim relates is later than the third week following that in which the claim is made.
@ref sch 10 para 1(1) and (2) (src:5657-5658)
GIVEN place IS A `sch 10 para 1 Place`
      `the number of weeks by which the week to which the claim relates falls after the week in which the claim is made` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 1 the person is the one entitled` MEANS
    IF `the number of weeks by which the week to which the claim relates falls after the week in which the claim is made` GREATER THAN 3
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall not confer any priority" says only that this paragraph does not decide; the later paragraphs do
    ELSE CONSIDER place
         WHEN `sch 10 para 1 the person has already been awarded child benefit when the other claims` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `sch 10 para 1 the person is the one claiming` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the latter shall be entitled"

§§ `Paragraph 2 -- person having the child or qualifying young person living with him`

-- 2: "Subject to paragraph 1 above, as between a person entitled for any week by virtue of paragraph (a) of subsection (1) of section 143 above and a person entitled
-- by virtue of paragraph (b) of that subsection the former shall be entitled." The two section 143 answers are seam S33.
-- src:5660 | Subject to paragraph 1 above, as between a person entitled for any week by virtue of paragraph (a) of subsection (1) of section 143 above and a person entitled by virtue of paragraph (b) of that subsection the former shall be entitled.
@ref sch 10 para 2 (src:5660)
GIVEN `paragraph 1 decides between them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 143(1)(a) the person is entitled for the week by virtue of paragraph (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 143(1)(b) the person is entitled for the week by virtue of paragraph (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person is entitled for the week by virtue of paragraph (a) of section 143(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person is entitled for the week by virtue of paragraph (b) of section 143(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 2 the person is the one entitled` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `paragraph 1 decides between them`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to paragraph 1 above"
        IF `s 143(1)(a) the person is entitled for the week by virtue of paragraph (a)` AND `the other person is entitled for the week by virtue of paragraph (b) of section 143(1)`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 143(1)(b) the person is entitled for the week by virtue of paragraph (b)` AND `the other person is entitled for the week by virtue of paragraph (a) of section 143(1)`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the former shall be entitled"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as between a person entitled ... by virtue of paragraph (a) ... and a person entitled by virtue of paragraph (b)"

§§ `Paragraph 3 -- opposite-sex spouses or civil partners`

-- 3: "Subject to paragraphs 1 and 2 above, as between a man and woman who are married to, or civil partners of, each other and are residing together, the woman shall be entitled."
-- src:5662 | Subject to paragraphs 1 and 2 above, as between a man and woman who are married to, or civil partners of, each other and are residing together, the woman shall be entitled.
@ref sch 10 para 3 (src:5662)
GIVEN `paragraph 1 or 2 decides between them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person and the other person are a man and a woman who are married to, or civil partners of, each other and are residing together` IS A BOOLEAN
      sex IS A Sex
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 3 the person is the one entitled` MEANS
    IF `paragraph 1 or 2 decides between them` OR NOT `the person and the other person are a man and a woman who are married to, or civil partners of, each other and are residing together`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to paragraphs 1 and 2 above, as between a man and woman who are married to, or civil partners of, each other and are residing together"
    ELSE CONSIDER sex
         WHEN Woman THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN Man THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the woman shall be entitled"

§§ `Paragraph 4 -- parents`

-- 4(1): "Subject to paragraphs 1 to 3 above, as between a person who is and one who is not a parent of the child or qualifying young person the parent shall be entitled."
-- src:5664 | (1) Subject to paragraphs 1 to 3 above, as between a person who is and one who is not a parent of the child or qualifying young person the parent shall be entitled.
@ref sch 10 para 4(1) (src:5664)
GIVEN `paragraphs 1 to 3 decide between them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a parent of the child or qualifying young person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person is a parent of the child or qualifying young person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 4(1) the person is the one entitled` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `paragraphs 1 to 3 decide between them`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to paragraphs 1 to 3 above"
        IF `the person is a parent of the child or qualifying young person` AND NOT `the other person is a parent of the child or qualifying young person`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (NOT `the person is a parent of the child or qualifying young person`) AND `the other person is a parent of the child or qualifying young person`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the parent shall be entitled"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as between a person who is and one who is not a parent"

-- 4(2): "Subject as aforesaid, as between two persons residing together who are parents of the child or qualifying young person but do not fall within paragraph 3, the mother shall
-- be entitled." If both parents are mothers, or neither is, the sub-paragraph names no one.
-- src:5665 | (2) Subject as aforesaid, as between two persons residing together who are parents of the child or qualifying young person but do not fall within paragraph 3, the mother shall be entitled.
@ref sch 10 para 4(2) (src:5665)
GIVEN `paragraphs 1 to 3 decide between them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person and the other person are residing together and are both parents of the child or qualifying young person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the mother of the child or qualifying young person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person is the mother of the child or qualifying young person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 4(2) the person is the one entitled` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `paragraphs 1 to 3 decide between them` OR NOT `the person and the other person are residing together and are both parents of the child or qualifying young person`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject as aforesaid, as between two persons residing together who are parents ... but do not fall within paragraph 3"
        IF `the person is the mother of the child or qualifying young person` AND NOT `the other person is the mother of the child or qualifying young person`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (NOT `the person is the mother of the child or qualifying young person`) AND `the other person is the mother of the child or qualifying young person`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the mother shall be entitled"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sub-paragraph names the mother and no one else

§§ `Paragraph 5 -- other cases`

-- 5: "As between persons not falling within paragraphs 1 to 4 above, such one of them shall be entitled as they may jointly elect or, in default of election, as the Secretary of
-- State may in his discretion determine." 6(1): an election "shall be made in the prescribed manner". The Secretary of State's discretion is a judgment taken as an input.
DECLARE `sch 10 para 5 Election` IS ONE OF
    `sch 10 para 5 the persons have jointly elected the person`
    `sch 10 para 5 the persons have jointly elected the other person`
    `sch 10 para 5 the persons have not jointly elected`

-- src:5667 | As between persons not falling within paragraphs 1 to 4 above, such one of them shall be entitled as they may jointly elect or, in default of election, as the Secretary of State may in his discretion determine.
@ref sch 10 para 5 (src:5667)
GIVEN `paragraphs 1 to 4 decide between them` IS A BOOLEAN
      election IS A `sch 10 para 5 Election`
      `the election was made in the prescribed manner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State has determined, in default of election, that the person is the one entitled` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 5 the person is the one entitled` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `paragraphs 1 to 4 decide between them`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "As between persons not falling within paragraphs 1 to 4 above"
        IF (NOT `the election was made in the prescribed manner`) AND (election EQUALS `sch 10 para 5 the persons have jointly elected the person` OR election EQUALS `sch 10 para 5 the persons have jointly elected the other person`)
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): 6(1) says an election "shall be made in the prescribed manner" and does not say what follows when it is not
        IF `the election was made in the prescribed manner` AND election EQUALS `sch 10 para 5 the persons have jointly elected the person`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the election was made in the prescribed manner` AND election EQUALS `sch 10 para 5 the persons have jointly elected the other person`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "such one of them shall be entitled as they may jointly elect"
        OTHERWISE `the Secretary of State has determined, in default of election, that the person is the one entitled`   -- NOTHING when no determination has been made: "as the Secretary of State may in his discretion determine"

§§ `Paragraph 6 -- supplementary`

-- 6(1): "Any election under this Schedule shall be made in the prescribed manner." The text does not say what follows when it is not, so neither branch is a "no".
-- 6(2): regulations may provide exceptions and modifications (inert, machinery).
-- src:5669 | (1) Any election under this Schedule shall be made in the prescribed manner.
@ref sch 10 para 6(1) (src:5669)
GIVEN `the election was made in the prescribed manner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 10 para 6(1) the election is an election under this Schedule` MEANS
    IF `the election was made in the prescribed manner`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall be made in the prescribed manner" is a necessary condition, not the whole of validity
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "shall be made in the prescribed manner" states a duty and not a consequence
